Summary: Shades!  But not the monster kind.
Keywords: protection from blinding

I've posted this here before, but I'd like to see what people think about it.
New item:  a pair of spectacles.  A tool, like a blindfold.  Could have
them be sunglasses.  They provide protection from most types of blinding,
including magic trap and lightning flashes, yellow light explosions, spit
venoms, Archon radiance, etc. but *not* from potions of blindness (although
not sure about *thrown* potions of blindness, since the effect seems to be
from inhaling the vapor, not from a splash).  Cursed ones blind the wearer
and won't come off, just like a blindfold;  normal ones make any room look
dark, even if it's lit/if a lantern is carried;  blessed ones either don't
make the room dark, or give the wearer a +1 charisma, or both.  (After all,
shades *are* cool).  Could even make mirrored shades, which reflect gaze
attacks and protect the wearer from them (so you could fight Medusa while
looking at her!!!).  I thought that perhaps making spectacles a worn item,
basically a new location for armor, might be cool, as they could then be
enchanted to provide armor value like a Hawaiian shirt, but others have
convinced me that they should be a tool like the blindfold (of course, if
they're an armor item, mirrored shades could be enchanted to give a higher
bonus to charisma, like a helm of brilliance...).  Well,  am I off my rocker,
or does this sound like an interesting idea?

